SIM-16: treat a negative pump speed from a pattern as closed

A pump's speed pattern is applied through setlinksetting() without a
range check. A negative factor left the pump OPEN with a negative speed,
pumpcoeff() took pow() of it, and the NaN flow survived until the end of
the run. Controls, rules and EN_setlinkvalue already reject negative
speeds, but a pattern can also drive demands and can be edited at any
time, so clamp the speed to 0 where it is applied: the pump closes, and
reopens at the next positive factor.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-16_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..dfaf2a0 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -452,8 +452,10 @@ void  setlinksetting(Project *pr, int index, double value, StatusType *s,
     LinkType t = link->Type;
 
     // For a pump, status is OPEN if speed > 0, CLOSED otherwise
+    // (a negative speed, e.g. from a pattern, counts as 0)
     if (t == PUMP)
     {
+        if (value < 0.0) value = 0.0;
         *k = value;
         if (value > 0 && *s <= CLOSED)
         {
